  "critique": "The current design is a victim of 'Dark Mode UI' fatigue. It reads like a generic settings menu or a dashboard widget rather than a tactile puzzle game. The visual language is flat and anonymous; the 'walls' are merely black squares with thin borders, lacking any sense of mass or obstruction. The 'Iron' in the title is betrayed by the lack of texture—the crates look like flat gray tiles rather than heavy objects to be pushed. The 'Flux' is reduced to a standard cyan glow, missing an opportunity for dynamic energy. The grid lines are too prominent, creating a 'spreadsheet' feel that competes with the gameplay elements rather than framing them. The controls legend at the bottom is purely functional and visually dead, breaking the immersion of the game world.",
  "suggestion": "Transform the board from a flat grid into a tactile, industrial surface. Replace the black wall squares with heavy, textured materials (riveted steel or concrete) that cast deep shadows to create a sense of depth and enclosure. Give the crates a distinct 'Iron' identity—add bevels, scratches, or a metallic sheen so they feel heavy and physical. Make the 'Flux' (player) and the Goal (door) the primary light sources in a dark environment; use volumetric lighting or bloom effects to make them pop against the matte background. Replace the thin grid lines with subtle surface imperfections or panel gaps. Finally, integrate the controls into the aesthetic—perhaps as etched markings on the floor or a holographic projection—rather than standard UI buttons."
}
